__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
# Downloaded dataset payloads, wherever they land.  But `lifelong_ood/data/` is a PYTHON PACKAGE
# that happens to be named data, and this rule silently swallowed it: its `__init__.py` was never
# committed, so a fresh clone could not import `lifelong_ood.data` at all, and every new module
# added there (multiobject.py) was dropped by `git add` with only a hint to say so.  Re-admit the
# package, keep excluding the payloads inside it.
data/
!lifelong_ood/data/
lifelong_ood/data/MNIST/
results/*.png
results/*.json
# ...except the pooled summary: every figure and every table is generated from it, so
# tracking it lets a fresh clone run `bash reproduce.sh figures` without 12 GPU-hours.
results/*.npz
slurm-*.out
.DS_Store
# slurm logs are noise, but the JOB SCRIPTS define how published results were produced and have
# to travel with the repo.  A parent directory that is excluded is never descended into, so the
# re-include has to be staged: exclude the contents, re-admit the jobs dir, exclude ITS contents,
# re-admit the scripts.
slurm/*
results/cache/
experiments/slurm/
slurm/*
!slurm/jobs/
slurm/jobs/*
!slurm/jobs/*.sbatch
figures/*_smoke.png
figures/*cscale*.png
figures/*pairscale*.png
figures/archive
figures/initial/archive

# Superseded figures. Kept in the tree because each cost GPU time and one that turns out to be
# wanted is then a `git mv` away -- but out of git, because they are dead weight in a clone and a
# reader opening figures/ should see the argument, not its history.
figures/archive/
# ...and the path they ACTUALLY live at.  Every figure moved under `figures/initial/` when
# `figures/vla/` was created, and this rule -- anchored, so `figures/archive/` matches nothing --
# quietly stopped applying.  56 MB across 34 superseded figures stayed tracked for weeks against
# the intent stated directly above it.  A gitignore rule that silently matches nothing is the same
# failure mode as a test that silently asserts nothing.
figures/initial/archive/
# ...and where that untracked pile physically landed when figures/initial moved to the archive.
archive/2026-09-pre-rework/figures/initial/archive/
